      "writtenOn": "2022-06-29T14:52:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is a graphite-only function, I\u0027d prefer to stick with the graphite-oriented types. I think we can just have it be:\n\n   std::pair\u003cRect, Transform\u003e boundsAndDeviceMatrix(const Transform\u0026 currentLocalToDevice, SkPoint drawOrigin) const;\n   \nThere is a separate battle for SkPoint vs. SkV2 (semi hand-in-hand with the SkMatrix vs. SkM44), but SkPoint has less baggage compared to SkMatrix, and the text subrun code already has everything in SkPoint.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1153,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1154,
        "endChar": 87
