      "message": "SkMatrix::invert and SkM44::invert have slightly different precision and don\u0027t 100% agree on what\u0027s singular. If we can stay in SkM44 throughout this, I\u0027d prefer that, since that\u0027s what sits under Transform.\n\nIf Transform gets moved to src/core, we could make a case that the subrun should just store that instead, since it remembers the inverse matrix or if it was singular. Then the view difference would simply be: `viewDifference \u003d Transform(currentLocalToDevice.matrix() * fInitialPositionMatrix.inverse());`.",
